# ==============================================================================
# SNAP Automation Crontab Example
# ==============================================================================
# This file contains example crontab entries for uutils automation services.
# Do NOT copy-paste blindly. Choose the python path and scripts that apply.
# Use `crontab -e` to install these.
#
# Each service command is wrapped with `flock -n` to prevent multiple
# instances of the same script from running simultaneously.
#
# Cron runs with a minimal PATH (usually /usr/bin:/bin), so use absolute paths
# such as /usr/sbin/logrotate, or set PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin
# at the top of the crontab.

# NOTE: Variable assignments in a crontab do not expand variables like $HOME.
# The shell used by cron runs commands using /bin/sh, so we use $HOME in the
# command lines below which will expand correctly at execution time.

# 1. Job-queue watcher
# The watcher is a long-lived daemon, not a periodic job.
# It should be started at reboot or manually, NOT on a periodic schedule.
# Ensure this line is in your crontab for auto-start:
# @reboot /dfs/scratch0/brando9/bin/start_watcher_at_reboot.sh
# For a manual start (the script creates its own tmux session "job_watcher"):
# bash $HOME/ultimate-utils/py_src/uutils/job_scheduler_uu/start_watcher.sh

# 2. Logrotate (runs daily to rotate logs generated by the services)
# @daily /usr/sbin/logrotate --state ~/.config/uutils_automation/logrotate.state ~/.config/uutils_automation/logrotate.conf >> ~/logs/uutils_automation/logrotate.log 2>&1

# ==============================================================================
# Messaging / Integration Services
# ==============================================================================
# What exists in uutils today (all default to dry-run; nothing is sent without --send):
#   One-shot send CLIs, usable as building blocks inside your own cron job:
#     python -m uutils.slack_uu send ...        (~/keys/slack_bot_token.txt)
#     python -m uutils.zulip_uu send ...        (~/keys/zuliprc)
#     python -m uutils.sms_uu send ...          (~/keys/twilio_credentials.json or ~/keys/tasker_autoremote_key.txt)
#     python -m uutils.instagram_uu post ...    (~/keys/instagram_credentials.json)
#     python -m uutils.facebook_uu post ...     (~/keys/facebook_credentials.json)
#   Libraries without a CLI: emailing.py (~/keys/gmail_app_password.txt),
#     discord_uu.py (~/keys/discord_webhook_url.txt), twitter_uu.py (~/keys/twitter_api_config.json).
#   Long-running daemons (run in tmux, not cron): the WhatsApp auto-reply webhook bot
#     (uutils.whatsapp_uu.run_whatsapp_bot; needs a public webhook URL and ~/keys/whatsapp_api_config.json)
#     and the email reply bot in experiments/03_email_reply_bot/.
#   There is no periodic sync job yet (for example Google Drive image sync); a new
#   <service>_job.py would be needed first.
#
# Template for a periodic job once one exists (flock prevents overlapping runs):
# */10 * * * * flock -n ~/.config/uutils_automation/<service>.lock ~/uv_envs/veribench/bin/python $HOME/ultimate-utils/scripts/snap_automation/<service>_job.py >> ~/logs/uutils_automation/<service>.log 2>&1
